hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17740","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Hashim, meaning Ibn al-Barid, narrated to us who said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil narrated to us, from Ibn Jabir who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after he had poured water. I said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah, but he did not reply to me. I said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah, but he did not reply to me. I said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah, but he did not reply to me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went walking and I was behind him, until he entered upon his baggage, and I entered the mosque and sat down gloomy and sad. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to me after he had purified himself, and said: Upon you be peace and the mercy of Allah, upon you be peace and the mercy of Allah, upon you be peace and the mercy of Allah. Then he said: Shall I not tell you, O Abdullah ibn Jabir, of the best sura in the Quran. I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Recite: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds, until you seal it."
